WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:01.670 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  bagpipes welcomed ukraine fans to hamden  park for their world cup qualifying  knockout against scotland  the winners would go one game away from  qualifying for qatar 2022  first and second generation ukrainians  travelled from all over the world to see  their team's first competitive game  since the russian invasion  i think that it will be even an  emotional game for ukrainian fans and  all ukrainian fans in ukraine as well  the community really  coming together showing the support  wearing the flag it's quite a nice and  comforting feeling ukraine gets  represented by its national team at this  time  it's probably the most important thing  in the world  for us at the end there is a game of  football and obviously scotland do want  to win but it does feel slightly bigger  than that  postponed from its original date in  march the match began with applause for  the ukrainian anthem from the scottish  crowd  kickoff sympathy was forgotten but  ukraine didn't need it  they created the early chances and with  half an hour gone they got their  reward andre yarmolenko getting them a  step closer to qatar for so much tonight  straight after half time the world cup  got closer still  just there with the header  [Applause]  with a simple header 2 nil ukraine  look what it means to him  the scots thought they had got back in  it but john mcginn incredibly headed  wide  wide  with just over 10 minutes to go a  goalkeeping error lets scotland make it  2-1  colin mcgregor's shot just going over  the line just creeps over the line i'll  imagine yes  but with the final kick of the match  artem dovbruck raced through to seal a  3-1 victory  and give ukrainians a rare moment of joy  in a tragic few months  [Applause]  i have no emotions to be honest with you  all of my emotions are left on the  football pitch this victory was not for  me it wasn't for the team members it was  for our country so it was a huge win for  ukraine  ukraine's players and fans have waited a  long time for this fixture but they've  harnessed the emotions of what's  happening to their country to bring  their world cup dream tantalizingly  close  paul reese al jazeera glasgow

